                <pb facs="0541" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg407"/>

                <head>No. 272.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Maury to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 29, 1887</date>.
                        (Received January 30, 1888.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    communication, received yesterday, from Señor Carlos Holguin, minister of
                    foreign affairs, relating to the claim of the Panama Railway Company to
                    exclusive telegraphic rights across the Isthmus, with a translation of the
                    same.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dabney H. Maury.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d272-a1.xml" xpointer="d272-a1"/>
            </div>
